{"class":"classes.MySimpleThreshold","values":{"description":"Very simple thresholder","headless":true,"menu":[{"label":"DeveloperPlugins"},{"label":"MyThresholder"}],"type":"org.scijava.command.Command"}}{"class":"classes.MyFragmentDemoPlugin","values":{"description":"One way to add new ImageJ plugins to KNIME is to wrap them with fragments of org.knime.knip.imagej.core . The automatic plugin retriev mechanism will discover the plugins, parse the annotations and add them as KNIME nodes. However the java compiler settings of the fragment project have to be adjusted to meet the requirements of the sezpoz library. For more details see sezpoz.java.net => Notes => Eclipse-specific notes or inspect the MyFragmentDemoPlugin.","headless":true,"menu":[{"label":"DeveloperPlugins"},{"label":"MyFragmentDemoPlugin"}],"type":"org.scijava.command.Command"}}{"class":"classes.MyPlugin","values":{"description":"tests various parameter types","headless":true,"menu":[{"label":"DeveloperPlugins"},{"label":"MyPlugin"}],"type":"org.scijava.command.Command"}}